  "decision": "not promoted: both conservative exact-seat candidates regressed on the predeclared paired development gate",
  "conclusion": "The full-slate contract fixes the positive-only selection bias of the preceding action-Q experiment and scales supervision to 51,200 replayable states and 4,961,912 legal alternatives. Both candidates reduced held-out target KL while preserving 98.4-99.5% of source top choices, but measured pair accuracy moved by only 0.01-0.19 percentage points and neither candidate improved game outcomes. Scale 1 and scale 2 each finished 18-20 against the frozen source over the same 100 paired maps, so neither earned fresh confirmation games.",
  "next_experiment": "Replace the globally linear action head update with a nonlinear state-action residual scorer trained against calibrated deeper-search returns. Validate its ability to rank PUCT-visited alternatives on game-disjoint states before routing any candidate into a paired outcome scout."
